    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d974">

                <pb facs="0890" n="882" sameAs="frus:frus1940v04/pg882"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">793.94/15960: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Japan</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Grew</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Tokyo</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1940-06-18T20:00:00+09:00">June 18, 1940—8
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received June 18—9:14 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>463. Our 452, June 15, 6 p.m.<anchor n="82" xml:id="d974-f1"/> We have been
                    informed by an American correspondent that the Foreign Office has already given
                    to the press an announcement concerning the reply to our representations made on
                    June 15 as reported in our telegram under reference concerning the bombing of
                    Chungking. Following is our translation of the Foreign Office note which was
                    received late this afternoon:</p>
                <p>[Here follows text of Japanese note No. 121, June 18, printed in <ref
                        target="frus:frus1931-41v01/pg_694"><hi rendition="#italic">Foreign
                            Relations</hi>, Japan, 1931–1941, volume I, page 694</ref>.]</p>
                <p>Repeated to Shanghai. Shanghai please repeat to Chungking, Peiping.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Grew</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d974-f1" n="82" xml:id="d974-f1-content">
                <p>This telegram reported the Ambassador’s representations; see his memorandum of
                    June 15, <ref target="frus1931-41v01#pg_692"><hi rendition="#italic">Foreign
                            Relations</hi>, Japan, 1931–1941, Vol. <hi rendition="#small-caps"
                            >i</hi>, p. 692</ref>.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
